WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:02.836
-Congress has been rocked

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:05.338
by its own sexual
misconduct allegations this week

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:06.406
with Senator Al Franken

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:07.974
being accused
of sexual harassment.

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:11.410
Yet more women coming forward to
accuse Alabama Senate candidate

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.646
Roy Moore of sexually assaulting
them as teenagers.

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:15.915
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:20.186
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.722
The avalanche
of sexual harassment allegations

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:25.291
in the last few weeks has shown
us that predatory behavior

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:28.528
is everywhere in virtually
every aspect of society --

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.697
in the news business,
in entertainment,

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:31.798
and in politics.

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:34.134
Every day,
there are more revelations,

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:35.635
and this week,
we started to get a sense

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:39.638
of just how pervasive sexual
harassment is in Congress, too.

00:00:39.638 --> 00:00:43.743
-There are two members
of Congress,

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:48.681
Republican and Democrat,
right now, who serve,

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:52.284
who have been subject to review,

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:54.186
or not have been
subject to review,

00:00:54.186 --> 00:00:56.255
but have engaged
in sexual harassment.

00:00:56.255 --> 00:00:59.725
These harasser propositions,
such as,

00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:01.628
"Are you going
to be a good girl?"

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:04.196
to perpetrators
exposing their genitals,

00:01:04.196 --> 00:01:06.065
to victims having
their private parts

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.833
grabbed on the House floor.

00:01:07.833 --> 00:01:09.102
-That is awful.

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.736
I'd say Congress
is full of dicks,

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:13.006
but most of them
look more like ball sacks.

00:01:13.006 --> 00:01:14.207
[ Laughter ]

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:16.141
And today, we also learned,
yet again,

00:01:16.141 --> 00:01:17.510
as if more evidence was needed,

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.011
that this is not
a partisan problem.

00:01:19.011 --> 00:01:20.212
There are sexual harassers

00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:22.348
of all political persuasions
in both parties.

00:01:22.348 --> 00:01:24.017
Take Minnesota Senator
Al Franken.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:27.220
Today, an anchor for KABC
in Los Angeles

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.488
said, "Senator Al Franken
kissed and groped me

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:32.792
without my consent
during a USO tour in 2006,"

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.893
and shared this photo
of Franken groping her

00:01:34.893 --> 00:01:36.028
while she was asleep.

00:01:36.028 --> 00:01:37.297
That is horrifying.

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:39.899
And she's wearing Army gear
because it's a USO tour,

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.701
but, honestly,
who could blame women

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.536
if they started
wearing military gear

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.304
whenever they're around men?

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:47.507
"Where are you going
in a helmet and a flak jacket?"

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.942
"The subway."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.942 --> 00:01:53.412
This is a pervasive problem that
affects every aspect of society

00:01:53.412 --> 00:01:54.813
and every political party,

00:01:54.813 --> 00:01:56.015
and everyone
should be held accountable,

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.084
from Al Franken to Roy Moore
to Bill Clinton

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:00.219
to the current President
of the United States.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:03.055
And yet amid all of this,
there are still Republicans

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:06.259
defending Moore, their nominee
for Senate in Alabama,

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.927
who, of course, has been accused

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.062
of sexually assaulting
underage girls.

00:02:10.062 --> 00:02:13.333
Take, for example,
Alabama Congressman, Mo Brooks,

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.934
who said he still plans
to support Moore

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:18.604
because the conservative agenda
is vastly more important

00:02:18.604 --> 00:02:20.372
than contested
sexual allegations

00:02:20.372 --> 00:02:22.008
from four decades ago.

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:23.909
An ABC reporter
tried to ask Brooks

00:02:23.909 --> 00:02:25.678
if he believes
the very credible accounts

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.747
of the women who accused Moore
of sexual assault,

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:31.117
and Brooks literally ran away
from him during the interview.

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:34.154 line:0%
[ Shoes tapping ]

00:02:44.763 --> 00:02:47.199
"Bad day to wear my tap shoes."

00:02:47.199 --> 00:02:54.807
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.743
I'd tell Mo Brooks
to go to hell,

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:58.845
but it looks like
that's where he's trying to get.

00:02:58.845 --> 00:03:00.213
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.615
That whole scene reminds me
of the M.C. Escher drawing

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.150
titled "The Chicken [bleep]"

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.585
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.753
Of course, part of the reason
Republicans are so desperate

00:03:07.753 --> 00:03:09.488
to ignore questions about Moore

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:11.690
is that even the ones who say
they believe his accusers

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.560
can't explain why they don't
also believe the women

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:17.163
who have accused President Trump
of sexual assault.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:19.231
A reporter for
The Huffington Post

00:03:19.231 --> 00:03:21.967
valiantly tried to get
Wyoming Senator Mike Enzi

00:03:21.967 --> 00:03:24.504
to answer that question,
but Enzi wouldn't budge.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:48.294
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:53.699
You've got to admire --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:55.701
You've got to admire
The Huffington Post's effort.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.370
Reporters should just
keep doing that

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:59.104
until Republicans
answer the questions.

00:03:59.104 --> 00:04:01.374
"Look, I just want to talk
about building a wall."

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:03.208
"Okay. should we build a wall

00:04:03.208 --> 00:04:05.211
between teenagers
and Roy Moore?"

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:06.712
[ Laughter ]

00:04:06.712 --> 00:04:08.915
A reporter for NBC News
similarly tried

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:10.416
to get an answer about Moore

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.551
from Arkansas Republican Senator
Tom Cotton with no luck.

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:14.254
Here's that transcript.

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.967
So, technically,
the elevators had more to say

00:04:28.967 --> 00:04:31.070
in that transcript
than Tom Cotton.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:34.573
So, hey, elevator, do you think
Roy Moore should drop out?

00:04:34.573 --> 00:04:37.810
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:42.115
The refusal by many Republicans,
including the President,

00:04:42.115 --> 00:04:43.716
to discuss Moore's situation

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:45.885
comes as we keep
getting information

00:04:45.885 --> 00:04:47.953
about how creepy
his behavior was.

00:04:47.953 --> 00:04:49.855
Earlier this week,
it was reported that Moore

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:54.126
was actually banned from
the Gadsden Mall and the YMCA.

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:57.896
He got banned from the YMCA
despite dressing exactly

00:04:57.896 --> 00:04:59.231
like one of The Village People.

00:04:59.231 --> 00:05:01.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:04.971
Now, yesterday, on MSNBC,
Moore's lawyer, Trenton Garmon,

00:05:04.971 --> 00:05:07.706
tried to dispute the claim that
Moore was banned from the mall,

00:05:07.706 --> 00:05:10.042
but in the process,
he seemed to confirm

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:13.078
that there were, indeed,
complaints about his behavior.

00:05:13.078 --> 00:05:16.382
-I was engaged in litigation
with the Gadsden Mall.

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.684
It had a settlement
that was confidential.

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:21.020
I'm intimately familiar
with the procedures

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:24.991
inside of the Gadsden Mall,
and from what I have been told,

00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:27.293
has never been a list
with Roy Moore

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:28.561
banned from being at the mall.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:31.130
So they processed that out,
and they determined,

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.266
"No, whatever it is
that someone has said

00:05:33.266 --> 00:05:34.666
has made them uncomfortable,

00:05:34.666 --> 00:05:37.303
we don't find it to be worthy
to put them on a list.

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:40.539
-Is it not cause for concern
that there would even be

00:05:40.539 --> 00:05:43.642
any sort of settlement
with the Gadsden Mall?

00:05:43.642 --> 00:05:46.678
Roy Moore was in his 30s.

00:05:46.678 --> 00:05:48.547
What type of settlement
would there be?

00:05:48.547 --> 00:05:50.316
-[ Clears throat ]
No, there was not

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.552
a settlement with Roy Moore,
had nothing to do --

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:53.618
Roy Moore has never had
a settlement

00:05:53.618 --> 00:05:55.020
with the Gadsden Mall.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:58.224
I'm talking about my personal
experience as a litigator.

00:05:58.224 --> 00:06:00.993
I have represented people
against the Gadsden Mall.

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:04.864
-Wait. You've been a lawyer in
other cases of People v. Mall?

00:06:04.864 --> 00:06:06.065
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:08.200
So I guess that
you've been banned from the mall

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.269
and need a lawyer,
Trenton Garmon is your man.

00:06:10.269 --> 00:06:12.204
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.204 --> 00:06:14.173
But the weirdest
part of the interview

00:06:14.173 --> 00:06:15.975
that Moore's lawyer
gave to MSNBC

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:18.110
came when he tried to defend
Moore's claim

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.879
that he always
asked for permission

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:21.781
from a girl's mother
before dating her.

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:23.883
Garmon tried to argue that
that kind of behavior

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.484
was common in other cultures,

00:06:25.484 --> 00:06:27.987
and threw in some gross racism
when he tried to cite

00:06:27.987 --> 00:06:32.225
MSNBC anchor Ali Velshi's
background to bolster his case.

00:06:32.225 --> 00:06:36.095
-Why would he need permission
from any of these girls' mothers

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:38.864
if they weren't underage?
-Not underage.

00:06:38.864 --> 00:06:40.433
-Sure, that's a good question.

00:06:40.433 --> 00:06:42.502
Culturally speaking,
I would say there's differences.

00:06:42.502 --> 00:06:44.937
I looked up
Ali's background there.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:47.406
And, wow, that's awesome
that you have got

00:06:47.406 --> 00:06:49.174
such a diverse background.

00:06:49.174 --> 00:06:50.542
It's really cool
to read through that.

00:06:50.542 --> 00:06:52.044
But point is this --

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:56.482
-What does Ali's background have
to do with dating a 14-year-old?

00:06:56.482 --> 00:06:58.450
-I'm not finished
with the context of it.

00:06:58.450 --> 00:06:59.919
-Well, please answer.

00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:03.289
What does Ali Velshi's
background have to do

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:06.826
with dating under-- children,
14-year-old girls?

00:07:06.826 --> 00:07:09.061
-Sure.
In other countries,

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:10.729
there's arrangement
through parents

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:12.898
for what we would refer to...
-Ali's from Canada.

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:14.433
-as consensual marriage.
-Ali's from Canada.

00:07:14.433 --> 00:07:15.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.534 --> 00:07:17.970
-So, either Trenton Garmon
is a racist,

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:21.707
or he thinks Canada
has arranged marriages.

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.709
And yet in spite
of all this damning evidence

00:07:23.709 --> 00:07:25.911
about Moore's predatory
and grotesque behavior,

00:07:25.911 --> 00:07:29.215
Trump still has said nothing
about what Moore should do.

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:31.249
In fact, yesterday,
he spoke at the White House

00:07:31.249 --> 00:07:33.819
about his trip to Asia,
and completely ignored questions

00:07:33.819 --> 00:07:35.421
about Moore from reporters.

00:07:35.421 --> 00:07:37.189
-America is back.

00:07:37.189 --> 00:07:39.925
And the future
has never looked brighter.

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:41.794
Thank you, God bless you,

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:44.830
and God bless
the United States of America.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.465
Thank you very much.
Thank you.

00:07:46.465 --> 00:07:47.867
Thank you all.

00:07:47.867 --> 00:07:50.369
-Should Roy Moore resign,
Mr. President?

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:51.937
Do you believe his accusers?

00:07:51.937 --> 00:07:54.606
Do you believe his accusers of
Roy Moore, Mr. President?

00:07:54.606 --> 00:07:56.943
Should he resign?

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:58.510
-If the future is so bright,

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:00.946
why do you look so bummed out
